carry_backtest prints +7.23 %/yr and QUOTABLE: False, with four of five
conditions met and one missing: rule_scored_on_an_untouched_window. The
gated rule's parameters were settled after 0018 with the whole corpus
visible. Nothing in +7.23 %/yr separates a carry edge that exists from one
that was fitted, and that separation is the whole distance between this
book and an asset.

Only a registered FORWARD holdout ticks that box and it needs settlements
that have not printed. tools/carry_walkforward.py is the strongest thing
obtainable today: refit every 30 days on what had printed by then, trade
the next 30 with that choice, never let a choice be scored on a settlement
it saw. 20,520 native simulations in 1.6 s — the first decision-grade use
of the 0039 core.

FIRST, A DEFECT (D18). The gated rule never reads an entry threshold:
may_open_gated decides on the EWMA, the cost of capital and the basis
budget. entry 0.1 bps and entry 2.4 bps both net $29,696.41 on 79 trades.
So 0039's "1,440 configurations" was 60 distinct rules printed 24 times,
the multiple-testing correction was fed a number describing the loop, and
ewma_alpha — a parameter the rule DOES have — was never searched at all.
Axes are now hold_days x negative_exit_prints x ewma_alpha.

WHAT IT FOUND, over 38 out-of-sample months:

  FROZEN (as shipped)     $26,489  +8.53 %/yr   57 trades  $6,353 fees  92%
  WALK-FORWARD (blind)    $42,600 +13.71 %/yr    6 trades    $779 fees  89%
  ORACLE (sees all)       $43,605 +14.04 %/yr    6 trades    $781 fees  92%

1. The surface is STABLE. Hindsight premium $1,004 of $43,605 — 2.3%. Four
   distinct cells chosen across 38 refits.
2. The shipped exit rule CHURNS, and now there is a number: 57 trades
   against 6 for the same exposure, $6,353 of fees against $779. D14, plain.
3. It churns because it will not sit through two bad days. Refit picks exit
   6 prints over the shipped 3; funding is positive 85.4% of prints.
4. They are DIFFERENT PRODUCTS. The cheap line holds 168 days per trade
   against 18, so its short must survive a +168% adverse excursion out of
   spot collateral. That is F4, and F4 is open.
5. Carry earns in SPIKES: the best 6 months of 38 carry 59-72% of the net;
   the median month is $326-443 on $100k.
6. AND NONE OF IT SURVIVES ITS OWN SEARCH WIDTH. Deflated Sharpe:

     walk-forward  +0.635 vs expected-max +0.663 under 20,520  z -0.272
     frozen (>=)   +0.495 vs expected-max +0.506 under    540  z -0.109

   The frozen line is charged one grid, not one trial: its constants were
   not pre-registered, so 540 is a floor and -0.109 is an UPPER bound on
   its evidence. Skew +3.2, kurtosis 15.1.

NOTHING IS ADOPTED. No winner is returned and the report carries no
"recommended" key; a test asserts it. Pasting exit=6 into carry_engine
because a search liked it is rule 20 and it is the path that cleared
funding_carry_fade_btc_v1 and then lost money forward.

The honest reading: the rule family is stable and the shipped exit rule is
measurably worse than the family's own centre, but this corpus is too short
and too spiky to establish that any of it beats zero. That is not a reason
to stop; it is why the forward holdout is now the work that matters.

Segment P&L is a difference of prefixes and telescopes to the bit — a test
asserts it for every additive term, so these lines are a decomposition of
one continuous run, not a stack of little backtests that restart flat.

